# Build outputs. The BPF objects are compiled from the C in bpf/ by
# `make bpf`; a committed object is one that can silently disagree with the
# source it was built from.
/bin/
/build/
*.test

# Coverage
coverage.out
coverage.html

# The assignment brief. Kept on disk, deliberately not published: it is in
# Portuguese, it is written for the author, and it carries a phase checklist
# whose boxes are unticked until the last one is done -- which reads, to
# anyone landing on the repository, as an abandoned project.
enunciado-latencia-ebpf.md

# Working notes across sessions: decisions and why, what this machine refuses
# to do, verifier rejections and their fixes, dead ends. The reasoning that
# earns its place ends up in the README as a decision; this is the scratch
# paper it came from.
NOTES.md

